/**
 * @file    CWbeaconWeb.ino
 * @brief   IoT-controlled HF CW (Morse code) beacon for NodeMCU v2 (ESP8266)
 *
 * @version 1.32
 * @author  Dr. IoT — IoT Lab @ IIS Cassata Gattapone, Gubbio, Italy
 * @link    https://doctoriot.wordpress.com/beacon-cw-14-mhz-3w/
 *
 * ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 * DESCRIPTION
 * ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 * Firmware for a 14 MHz (20 m band) amateur radio CW beacon based on the
 * NodeMCU v2 development board (ESP8266). The beacon continuously transmits
 * a Morse code message that contains:
 *   - The station call sign  (e.g. IA/IU0SZS)
 *   - A free-text QTC field  (e.g. 130YR PB14QV)
 *   - A 4-character Fletcher-16 CRC authentication code
 *
 * The CRC is computed over the current UTC timestamp concatenated with a
 * fixed salt ("25041874" — Marconi's birthday, April 25, 1874). This allows
 * any receiving station that knows the salt to verify the time and authenticity
 * of each transmission independently.
 *
 * The RF carrier is generated by a Si5351A clock IC driven over I2C and is
 * gated on/off synchronously with the LED indicator to key the Morse signal.
 *
 * ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 * CONNECTIVITY FEATURES
 * ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 *   Wi-Fi        : STA mode with automatic fallback to AP mode (SSID: CWbeacon-AP)
 *   Web server   : Status page + full configuration at http://<device-ip>/
 *   OTA update   : Firmware update via browser at http://<device-ip>/update
 *   Telegram bot : Real-time control and status via 15 bot commands
 *   NTP          : Time synchronization from pool.ntp.org, UTC, hourly resync
 *   Serial       : Diagnostic console at 115200 baud
 *
 * ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 * HARDWARE REQUIREMENTS
 * ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 *   - NodeMCU v2 (ESP8266, 4 MB flash)
 *   - Si5351A breakout board (Etherkit or compatible)
 *   - RF power amplifier (~3 W on 14 MHz)
 *   - Low-pass filter (20 m band, 7-element Chebyshev)
 *   - Status LED on GPIO14 / D5
 *   - 5 V USB or regulated DC supply (~500 mA)
 *
 * ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 * WIRING (NodeMCU v2 pin labels / GPIO numbers)
 * ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 *   Si5351A SDA  → D2  / GPIO4
 *   Si5351A SCL  → D1  / GPIO5
 *   Status LED   → D5  / GPIO14  (anode via resistor to 3.3 V)
 *
 * ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 * REQUIRED LIBRARIES (install via Arduino Library Manager)
 * ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 *   ArduinoJson        — JSON parsing (used indirectly by AsyncTelegram2)
 *   AsyncTelegram2     — Telegram Bot API client over BearSSL/TLS
 *   ESP8266 Arduino    — Core SDK (ESP8266WiFi, WebServer, HTTPUpdateServer …)
 *   NTPClient          — Network Time Protocol client
 *   Si5351             — Etherkit Si5351 driver (local copy: si5351.h / si5351.cpp)
 *   UnixTime           — Unix timestamp → calendar fields decomposition
 *
 * ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 * REVISION HISTORY
 * ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 *   1.32  Fixed beacon STOP request; added /info command to Telegram bot
 *   1.31  Fixed empty Wi-Fi password bug
 *   1.3   Added Telegram commands: /setspd, /setqrz, /setqrg, /setcal, /setmsg
 *   1.2   Added Telegram bot integration
 *   1.1   Web-based configuration interface
 *   1.0   First operating version
 */

